<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aksumite invasion of Kush</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 4th century CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aksumite invasion of Kush refers to military expeditions by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kingdom of Kush</a> in the c. 4th century CE, most notably under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ezana">King Ezana</a>. By then Kush was already weakened. The invasion is treated as one of the final blows in the decline of the Kushite Empire and its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meroe">Meroë</a>.</p></div>
